Z||000000||BAM-BAM||12-31-2001||11:48 AM||||New Years Resolution<P>   It's the beginning of a new year, 2002. It's also the time to begin a new way of living. I have been living in this rut of selfimposed turmoil long enough. There are some things that I must do in order to effect the necessary changes in my life and I am the only one who do them. I know from vast experience that I am the one who is responsible for my own happiness. I feel that if I can make me happy then those around me will surely follow, or fall by the way. This is not intended to be cruel, just a note to  myself to remain focused and on the correct path to happiness.<BR>   That being said, I want to list the changes that I expect and know will come to fruition. <P>1.) In 2002 and beyond, I resolve to love better, be a better husband and father and show compassion for those around me.<P>2.) In 2002 and beyond, I resolve to take control of my health issues including my needless overweight status and strive for a life of longevity and healthful bliss.<P>3.) In 2002 and beyond, I resolve to work harder and learn more about the craft that I have chosen and grown to enjoy<P>4.) In 2002 and beyond, I resolve to do my best to fill the roll of mentor and rolemodel for the youth of tomorrow; those who I will have the honor to influence and teach.<P>5.) In 2002 and beyond, I resolve to maintain my discipline for exactness and perfection in all tasks that I undertake and never compromise the purity of my artistic ability.<P>6.) In 2002 and beyond, I resolve to know God and his word in more detail, with greater understanding.<P>7.) in 2002 and beyond, I resolve to Love, Live and Enjoy life to it's fullest potential and reaffirm these resolutions every day. To start each day as though its the beginning and let yesterday's troubles fall into the past and look forward to tomorrows adventures! <P>    Though my resolutions may seem a bit lofty and child like. It is what I need in my life to complete me as a person and pave the way to a happy and joyful future. I have lived in the burdens of life and want only to enjoy life from now on. I want to work for my happiness and I don't expect it to be handed to me. I want the people around me to free from any burdens that I may levy and also free myself from their burdens. I enjoy the ability to help others based on my knowledge and experience and I'm willing to do what it takes as long as they are willing to help themselves. I think that is what I have lost in recent years; the knowledge that you can only be helped or help if you and others are willing to help yourselves. But I do resolve to do my best to do my best for myself and those that I love.<P>Don Bartlett, Dec. 31 2001-Jan. 1 2002 <P>------------------<BR>85GT 3.4L <BR>Eibachs and Poly's<BR>17" Konig Monsoons<BR>Kumho Ecstas<BR>Interior is all "Mike'd" up||||reg||1
